WEBVTT

1
00:00:57.500 --> 00:01:01.666


2
00:01:01.666 --> 00:01:04.583
<b>Just a few moments ago,</b>

3
00:01:04.583 --> 00:01:08.458
<b>Duryodhana mentioned</b>
<b>the name of Drupad’s son, Dhrishtadyumna.</b>

4
00:01:08.458 --> 00:01:11.500
<b>And tried to provoke Dronacharya.</b>

5
00:01:11.500 --> 00:01:13.750
<b>He was implying </b>

6
00:01:13.750 --> 00:01:20.583
<b>that Dronacharya had already made </b>
<b>a mistake once by teaching Dhrishtadyumna. </b>

7
00:01:20.583 --> 00:01:25.125
<b>He subtly warned Drona</b>
<b>not to repeat that mistake. </b>

8
00:01:25.125 --> 00:01:28.416
<b>To further stress his point, </b>

9
00:01:28.416 --> 00:01:36.541
<b>Duryodhana now starts naming all the warriors </b>
<b>who are preparing to fight on the Pandava side. </b>

10
00:01:36.541 --> 00:01:37.541
<b>He says</b>

11
00:01:37.541 --> 00:01:41.625
<b>"In this army (of the Pandavas), there are </b>
<b>great archers and warriors equal </b>

12
00:01:41.625 --> 00:01:47.125
<b>to Bhima and Arjuna in valor, </b>
<b>such as Yuyudhana, Virata, </b>

13
00:01:47.125 --> 00:01:49.250
<b>and the mighty Maharathi Drupada. </b>

14
00:01:49.250 --> 00:01:53.791
<b>Also present are Dhrishtaketu, Chekitana, </b>
<b>the powerful King of Kashi,</b>

15
00:01:53.791 --> 00:01:55.458
<b>Purujit, Kuntibhoja, </b>

16
00:01:55.458 --> 00:01:57.958
<b>and the most excellent among men, Shaibya.</b>

17
00:01:57.958 --> 00:01:59.875
<b>Along with them are the brave Yudhamanyu </b>

18
00:01:59.875 --> 00:02:04.750
<b>and the powerful Uttamauja,</b>
<b>the son of Subhadra (Abhimanyu), </b>

19
00:02:04.750 --> 00:02:10.125
<b>and the five sons of Draupadi</b>
<b>all these are Maharathis."</b>

20
00:02:10.750 --> 00:02:15.083


21
00:02:15.083 --> 00:02:15.791
<b>Here, </b>

22
00:02:15.791 --> 00:02:19.750
<b>Duryodhana is analyzing his enemy's army.</b>

23
00:02:19.750 --> 00:02:21.458
<b>First, Sanjaya</b>

24
00:02:21.458 --> 00:02:25.541
<b>sees the battle formation organized</b>
<b>by Dhrishtadyumna</b>

25
00:02:25.541 --> 00:02:32.041
<b>and then notices several mighty Maharathis</b>
<b>joining the Pandava army. </b>

26
00:02:32.041 --> 00:02:34.875
<b>But there’s something more. </b>

27
00:02:34.875 --> 00:02:43.166
<b>While listing all the warriors, Duryodhana</b>
<b>compares them to Arjuna and Bhima, </b>

28
00:02:43.166 --> 00:02:48.583
<b>as, in his estimation, these two are</b>
<b>his greatest threats.While Duryodhana </b>

29
00:02:48.583 --> 00:02:51.875
<b>is slightly less concerned about Arjuna,  </b>

30
00:02:51.875 --> 00:02:57.166
<b>believing that his friend Karna,</b>
<b>a skilled archer himself, </b>

31
00:02:57.166 --> 00:03:01.125
<b>will be able to defeat him, </b>

32
00:03:01.125 --> 00:03:03.250
<b>but here Bhima,</b>

33
00:03:03.250 --> 00:03:05.833
<b>Bhima is not just extremely strong, </b>

34
00:03:05.833 --> 00:03:08.500
<b>but he also has the burning desire</b>

35
00:03:08.500 --> 00:03:13.541
<b>to kill all the 100 Kauravas.</b>

36
00:03:13.541 --> 00:03:16.541
<b>Duryodhana is somewhat uncertain, </b>

37
00:03:16.541 --> 00:03:21.458
<b>as Bhima poses a significant challenge</b>
<b>for the Kauravas. </b>

38
00:03:21.458 --> 00:03:27.583
<b>However, in focusing so much on this problem, </b>
<b>Duryodhana makes a huge mistake.</b>

39
00:03:27.583 --> 00:03:29.125
<b>He </b>

40
00:03:29.125 --> 00:03:32.166
<b>overlooks Lord Krishna.</b>

41
00:03:32.166 --> 00:03:35.916
<b>Krishna doesn’t factor into</b>
<b>Duryodhana’s analysis</b>

42
00:03:35.916 --> 00:03:39.375
<b>because Krishna vowed not to take up arms. </b>

43
00:03:39.375 --> 00:03:43.833
<b>that war is only fought with weapons</b>
<b>and physical strength</b>

44
00:03:43.833 --> 00:03:49.250
<b>might cost Duryodhana dearly.</b>

45
00:03:49.250 --> 00:03:55.791
<b>Krishna's guidance and his presence with the</b>
<b>Pandavas give them immense mental strength.</b>

46
00:03:55.791 --> 00:03:59.291
<b>Having the right guidance and mental fortitude</b>

47
00:03:59.291 --> 00:04:04.916
<b>is far more powerful than </b>
<b>physical strength or weapons.</b>

48
00:04:05.583 --> 00:04:09.625
<b> </b>

49
00:04:09.625 --> 00:04:13.375
<b>This happens in our lives as well. </b>

50
00:04:13.375 --> 00:04:17.125
<b>We focus so much on small worries </b>

51
00:04:17.125 --> 00:04:20.625
<b>that we overlook the strength within us. </b>

52
00:04:20.625 --> 00:04:27.291
<b>In the rush of life,</b>
<b>we forget that the solution to every problem </b>

53
00:04:27.291 --> 00:04:29.541
<b>lies within us. </b>

54
00:04:29.541 --> 00:04:32.958
<b>We begin to think that </b>
<b>external success is true victory, </b>

55
00:04:32.958 --> 00:04:37.166
<b>but real victory is when we conquer the mind.</b>

56
00:04:37.166 --> 00:04:39.416
<b>For that, </b>

57
00:04:39.416 --> 00:04:41.166
<b>we need peace, </b>

58
00:04:41.166 --> 00:04:43.000
<b>mental awareness, </b>

59
00:04:43.000 --> 00:04:44.125
<b>truth,</b>

60
00:04:44.125 --> 00:04:46.458
<b>and righteousness</b>

61
00:04:46.458 --> 00:04:51.708
<b>Don’t make the mistake of ignoring these.</b>

62
00:04:51.708 --> 00:04:54.000
<b>And don't worry, </b>

63
00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:56.333
<b>the Bhagavad Gita is with you. </b>

64
00:04:56.333 --> 00:04:58.166
<b>Truth is with you. </b>

65
00:04:58.166 --> 00:05:00.083
<b>Righteousness is with you. </b>

66
00:05:00.083 --> 00:05:03.416
<b>Because I am right here with you, </b>

67
00:05:03.416 --> 00:05:06.416
<b>Your Krishna. </b>

68
00:05:06.416 --> 00:05:14.333
<b>Just don’t overlook me like Duryodhana did. </b>

69
00:05:14.333 --> 00:05:18.625
<b>Keep me with you, like the Pandavas did, </b>

70
00:05:18.625 --> 00:05:20.166
<b>and then </b>

71
00:05:20.166 --> 00:05:24.208
<b>victory in the battle of life will be yours.</b>

72
00:05:24.708 --> 00:05:28.916


73
00:05:28.916 --> 00:05:31.333
<b>If we ponder upon the question </b>

74
00:05:31.333 --> 00:05:38.416
<b>of when and where the animosity</b>
<b>between the Kauravas and Pandavas began, </b>

75
00:05:38.416 --> 00:05:46.166
<b>and what transpired that led to</b>
<b>the greatest war in India, the Mahabharata,</b>

76
00:05:46.166 --> 00:05:49.750
<b>we find that the Pandavas were born in the forest</b>

77
00:05:49.750 --> 00:05:53.416
<b>and after the death of their father Pandu,</b>

78
00:05:53.416 --> 00:05:58.166
<b>they came to Hastinapur with their mother Kunti.</b>

79
00:05:58.166 --> 00:06:01.708
<b>They lived with the Kauravas </b>

80
00:06:01.708 --> 00:06:06.500
<b>and studied under Guru Drona together. </b>

81
00:06:06.500 --> 00:06:12.958
<b>Children's minds are pure,</b>

82
00:06:12.958 --> 00:06:15.541
<b>free from any malice or ill-will. </b>

83
00:06:15.541 --> 00:06:17.916
<b>So, </b>

84
00:06:17.916 --> 00:06:23.083
<b>why did enmity arise between</b>
<b>the Kauravas and Pandavas?</b>

85
00:06:23.083 --> 00:06:26.291
<b>Children are impressionable, aren't they?</b>

86
00:06:26.291 --> 00:06:33.458
<b>The actions and words of their elders</b>
<b>greatly influence their lives. </b>

87
00:06:33.458 --> 00:06:37.166
<b>When no one provides</b>
<b>the right guidance for misconduct, </b>

88
00:06:37.166 --> 00:06:39.041
<b>unknowingly</b>

89
00:06:39.041 --> 00:06:44.583
<b>instills the poison of their hidden desires</b>
<b>into the minds of children, </b>

90
00:06:44.583 --> 00:06:47.458
<b>as Dhritarashtra did </b>

91
00:06:47.458 --> 00:06:50.666
<b>by remaining silent due to his own desires,</b>

92
00:06:50.666 --> 00:06:55.541
<b>it allowed the feeling </b>

93
00:06:55.541 --> 00:07:00.041
<b>that the Pandavas are inferior to</b>
<b>the Kauravas to take root in his sons' minds</b>

94
00:07:00.041 --> 00:07:02.958
<b>And what about the Kauravas' uncle, Shakuni? </b>

95
00:07:02.958 --> 00:07:06.791
<b>Did he not plot enough conspiracies? </b>

96
00:07:06.791 --> 00:07:10.833
<b>His wickedness also had an impact.</b>

97
00:07:10.833 --> 00:07:12.375
<b>Gradually, </b>

98
00:07:12.375 --> 00:07:14.916
<b>the childhood squabbles</b>

99
00:07:14.916 --> 00:07:19.375
<b>turned into animosity,</b>
<b>the fight for the throne, </b>

100
00:07:19.375 --> 00:07:27.333
<b>and ultimately, everyone found themselves</b>
<b>on the brink of the Mahabharata war.</b>

101
00:07:27.333 --> 00:07:31.125
<b>Children's minds are like fertile soil. </b>

102
00:07:31.125 --> 00:07:35.416
<b>If the seeds of envy,</b>
<b>hatred, and hostility are sown </b>

103
00:07:35.416 --> 00:07:41.208
<b>and watered with one's own desires,</b>
<b>what will grow is a dark plant that,</b>

104
00:07:41.208 --> 00:07:45.083
<b>when fully grown, becomes a tree of hatred. </b>

105
00:07:45.083 --> 00:07:49.625
<b>Such a tree is self-destructive, </b>

106
00:07:49.625 --> 00:07:57.083
<b>hollowing out its own trunk</b>
<b>and destroying its own roots. </b>

107
00:07:57.083 --> 00:08:01.041
<b>This is precisely what happened</b>
<b>to the Kauravas.</b>

108
00:08:01.041 --> 00:08:05.958
<b>Therefore, sow the seeds of harmony</b>
<b>in children's minds, </b>

109
00:08:05.958 --> 00:08:12.625
<b>nurture them with sensitivity,</b>
<b>and a plant of love will sprout, </b>

110
00:08:12.625 --> 00:08:17.666
<b>growing into a vast and dense tree </b>

111
00:08:17.666 --> 00:08:22.541
<b>under whose shade everyone will find joy.</b>

112
00:08:22.541 --> 00:08:26.583
<b>To do this, our first responsibility is to </b>

113
00:08:26.583 --> 00:08:32.500
<b>not impose our desires on children </b>

114
00:08:32.500 --> 00:08:37.083
<b>and to first make ourselves gentle</b>

115
00:08:37.083 --> 00:08:41.500
<b>The Bhagavad Gita</b>
<b>will support you in this endeavor.</b>

116
00:08:42.041 --> 00:08:46.000
<b> </b>

117
00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:48.041
<b>From a professional perspective, </b>

118
00:08:48.041 --> 00:08:54.166
<b>we learn not one but two lessons here: </b>

119
00:08:54.166 --> 00:08:56.958
<b>one from Duryodhana's competence </b>

120
00:08:56.958 --> 00:09:01.375
<b>and the other from his mistake.</b>

121
00:09:01.375 --> 00:09:03.041
<b>No matter what,</b>

122
00:09:03.041 --> 00:09:08.291
<b>Duryodhana is a capable warrior. </b>

123
00:09:08.291 --> 00:09:11.125
<b>He has closed the eyes of his mind, </b>

124
00:09:11.125 --> 00:09:20.458
<b>but at least with his physical eyes, he is first </b>
<b>assessing his battle situation at this moment.</b>

125
00:09:20.458 --> 00:09:23.083
<b>Outwardly, he may say anything, </b>

126
00:09:23.083 --> 00:09:33.250
<b>but he is trying to thoroughly gauge the strength</b>
<b>of each warrior standing on the enemy side.</b>

127
00:09:33.250 --> 00:09:39.125
<b>In any serious situation, rather than</b>
<b>being agitated and taking hasty action, </b>

128
00:09:39.125 --> 00:09:44.208
<b>it is more important</b>
<b>to first evaluate the situation. </b>

129
00:09:44.208 --> 00:09:50.833
<b>It is wise to act only after</b>
<b>assessment and planning.</b>

130
00:09:50.833 --> 00:09:52.916
<b>However, </b>

131
00:09:52.916 --> 00:09:57.666
<b>Duryodhana has also made a mistake here, </b>

132
00:09:57.666 --> 00:10:00.333
<b>and that is </b>

133
00:10:00.333 --> 00:10:03.041
<b>ignoring me. </b>

134
00:10:03.041 --> 00:10:06.250
<b>One who wears the spectacles of ego, </b>

135
00:10:06.250 --> 00:10:10.333
<b>how will they see the importance</b>
<b>of mental strength,</b>

136
00:10:10.333 --> 00:10:13.833
<b>counsel, and inner wisdom? </b>

137
00:10:13.833 --> 00:10:16.333
<b>How will they see me, </b>

138
00:10:16.333 --> 00:10:20.000
<b>who could have been his as well, </b>

139
00:10:20.000 --> 00:10:21.916
<b>but</b>

140
00:10:21.916 --> 00:10:28.000
<b>he was more interested in my army?</b>

141
00:10:28.000 --> 00:10:33.166
<b>In professional life too,</b>
<b>the right advice is most beneficial. </b>

142
00:10:33.166 --> 00:10:37.333
<b>The power of the mind is the supreme power. </b>

143
00:10:37.333 --> 00:10:40.000
<b>Don't be like Duryodhana. </b>

144
00:10:40.000 --> 00:10:42.708
<b>Recognize this power. </b>

145
00:10:42.708 --> 00:10:44.583
<b>Come, </b>

146
00:10:44.583 --> 00:10:46.541
<b>hold my hand.</b>

